schema: "0.4"
id: chalkboard-09-graded-projects
type: image
quality: high

# The Robot Learns — a terminal study CLI. Graded Projects — hands-on assignments submitted
# for rubric-based evaluation by a grader sub-agent, rendered as a chalkboard terminal. HERO
# screen (rendered side-by-side against workbench), so it must carry the chalkboard voice.
# Theme tenets: always-dark forest-green slate board, warm chalk-white hand-lettering, dusty
# colored-chalk accents used categorically (never neon), flat radius-0 board, dashed chalk
# rules + hand-drawn underline/circle for emphasis (never bold weight); error reinforced with
# an underline/icon since rose chalk is both a brand and the error hue.
# Palette: board green #2d4a2d, near-black board #1e2a1e, chalk-white #e8e4d8, sand-chalk
# #c8c0a8, yellow chalk #e8d44c, blue chalk #6cb4dc, rose chalk #e06060, sage chalk #50b878.

prompt:
  system: |
    You are a senior product designer rendering a high-fidelity UI mockup of a warm,
    always-dark TERMINAL session skinned as a professor's chalkboard — a single focused
    terminal window, not a web page and not a browser. The surface is a graded project report:
    the tutor has marked a hands-on assignment and drawn the feedback out on the board like a
    professor handing back work. Rubric comments are hand-lettered in a casual print-handwriting
    face; the overall score, article ids and technical values stay in a neat monospace. Emphasis
    is an underline, a drawn checkmark, or a chalk circle around the grade, never a bold weight.
    Colored chalk is dusty and desaturated, never neon. Flat board, square corners, dashed chalk
    rules, a faint dust of chalk texture.
  text: |
    A 16:9 high-fidelity mockup of a focused single-pane TERMINAL session — "The Robot
    Learns" — skinned as a dark green chalkboard, showing a graded project handed back. A plain
    dark forest-green terminal window with a thin flat title bar fills the whole frame, its
    green board surface acting as the terminal canvas — not a wooden-framed classroom blackboard
    on an easel. NO browser chrome, NO tabs, NO address bar, NO web page, NO wooden picture frame.

    OVERALL LAYOUT: three clear columns — a header band with the project title and its score
    on top, a dominant rubric feedback column on the left two-thirds, and a distinct citation
    column down the right third that must be present.

    The HEADER BAND carries the project title in display handwriting, "Build a spaced-repetition
    scheduler", and to the right a SCORE / RESULTS SUMMARY drawn as a big hand-circled grade in
    bright chalk, "87 / 100", looped with a chalk circle, plus a one-line verdict beneath in
    warm chalk, "Solid — your ease-factor update is off by one case".

    The dominant CENTER is the PROJECT RUBRIC FEEDBACK BLOCK — a vertical list of rubric
    criteria, each a row with the criterion name in chalk-white, a hand-drawn chalk checkmark in
    sage green or a small cross in rose, a short hand-lettered comment, and a small per-criterion
    mark in monospace, "Correctness 24/30", "Design 20/20", "Tests 18/25", "Docs 25/25". Rows are
    divided by dashed chalk rules. One row's correction is underlined in rose chalk with a small
    "watch this" margin note and a hand-drawn chalk arrow pointing at it, the rose reinforced by a
    small warning tick so it does not read as ordinary red chalk.

    The whole right third is a clearly visible citation column, headed by the hand-written
    label "cited from your board", listing four references to knowledge articles the grader
    drew on — each one a chalk-underlined link in dusty blue chalk with a monospace article id
    beside a short hand-lettered title: "kb-0231 · SM-2 scheduling", "kb-0198 · ease factors",
    "kb-0142 · review intervals", "kb-0077 · leitner boxes". This citation column is a required
    region and must be filled, not blank. A faint monospace status line at the very bottom reads
    "graded by tutor-agent · resubmit with /project submit".

    PALETTE & TYPE: a deep forest-green slate board as the canvas, one slightly lighter green
    panel where the score and citations lift; lettering in warm dusty chalk-white, secondary
    labels in dimmer sand-chalk. Marks and categories in sticks of dusty colored chalk — a soft
    rose-red for corrections, a sage green for passes, a dusty sky-blue for citations, a warm
    butter-yellow for the circled grade — all desaturated like real chalk, never bright or neon.
    Rubric comments hand-lettered in a casual print handwriting face; the score, ids and marks in
    a neat monospace.

    SHAPE & SURFACE: flat board with square corners, no rounded cards and no glossy panels;
    rows and regions divided by dashed chalk rules; the score is circled by hand in chalk, not
    boxed in a filled badge; a faint even dust of chalk grain and one soft eraser smudge.

    MOOD: warm, academic, personal — work handed back with care, the correction drawn out so it
    clicks, the best teacher you ever had.
  negative: "watermark, signature, lorem ipsum placeholder text, low-fidelity wireframe, monitor/device photograph framing, blurry, distorted UI, browser chrome, address bar, browser tabs, web page, rounded cards, glossy panels, neon or saturated colors, dry-erase whiteboard, pure white or light background, bold heavy type, wooden picture frame, easel, ornate frame, Windows or generic app title-bar buttons, empty right margin"

output:
  formats:
    - format: png
  dimensions:
    width: 1920
    height: 1080
    aspect_ratio: "16:9"

eval:
  pass_threshold: 0.72
  criteria:
    relevance: {weight: 3, description: "Matches Graded Projects: a project title with an overall score/results summary, a rubric feedback block of per-criterion rows with marks and comments, and a citation list of KB references — inside one terminal board"}
    theme_fidelity: {weight: 3, description: "Always-dark forest-green board, warm chalk-white handwriting comments + mono score/ids, dusty categorical colored-chalk marks (sage pass, rose correction, blue citation, yellow circled grade; no neon), hand-drawn checkmarks/circle/underline, flat square corners, dashed chalk rules — not generic UI defaults"}
    composition: {weight: 2, description: "Report-card hierarchy: circled score, dominant rubric column, slim citation margin, plausible real-product terminal layout"}
    technical: {weight: 2, description: "Sharp, correct 16:9 aspect, no artifacts"}
  reject_if:
    - "lorem ipsum or placeholder text visible"
    - "watermark or signature visible"
    - "wireframe-level fidelity instead of high-fidelity mockup"
    - "browser chrome, tabs, or address bar instead of a terminal window"
    - "neon or saturated colors, or a light/whiteboard background"

tags: [chalkboard, therobotlearns.com, screen-mockup, terminal, hero]
